    98	```
    99	Add note that `/design` commits logs to a standalone branch PR with `[skip ci]` and auto-merges with `--admin`.
   100	
   101	**9. `SECURITY.md`**
   102	Add note under design log section: all files from `DESIGN_TMPDIR` pass through `redact-tmpdir-paths.sh` + `redact-secrets.sh` before commit; coverage is best-effort; operators should avoid pasting API keys into /design prompts.
   103	
   104	### Approach
   105	
   106	**`[PLANNED]` prefix**: symmetric with the existing `[IN PROGRESS]`, `[DONE]`, `[STALLED]` lifecycle marker system. Adding `planned` as a new state to `tracking-issue-write.sh rename` requires touching 5 locations in that file (state_to_prefix, strip_lifecycle_prefix, error message, usage, CUR_CANON_PREFIXES case) and 1 in `lib-title-markers.sh` (insert_signal_marker). Both scripts are Bash 3.2-compatible; the new case follows existing patterns exactly.
   107	
   108	**Log publish script**: `scripts/design-log-publish.sh` does a direct copy of DESIGN_TMPDIR content with two-stage redaction (tmpdir paths first, then secrets). Manifest JSON is written by the script directly (not via `larch-log.sh init`) because `larch-log.sh commit` would hardcode the commit message without `[skip ci]`. The script is placed in `scripts/` (synthesis choice, 1-1 judge tie → fallback) for consistency with `larch-log-flush.sh`, `create-pr.sh`, `merge-pr.sh`.
   109	
   110	**Merge mechanism**: direct `gh pr merge --squash --admin --delete-branch` (synthesis choice, thesis debate truncated → fallback) because `merge-pr.sh` requires `mergeStateStatus in {CLEAN,UNSTABLE,HAS_HOOKS,BLOCKED}` and a `[skip ci]` PR may not reach CLEAN before the merge attempt. The `--admin` flag bypasses branch protection + CI gate. The `--delete-branch` flag cleans up the design branch after merge.
   111	
   112	**Step 5 ordering** (from discussion-round1.md): plan-block-write → rename [PLANNED] → design-log-publish → cleanup-tmpdir. Log flush must happen before cleanup because `cleanup-tmpdir.sh` removes DESIGN_TMPDIR.
   113	
   114	### Edge cases
   115	
   116	- **Rename failure**: `tracking-issue-write.sh rename` is best-effort; warning is printed but plan-write is already done and logs still flush.
   117	- **design-log-publish.sh failure**: best-effort; warning printed, cleanup still runs, `PLAN_WRITE_OK` already set.
   118	- **Default branch guard**: `design-log-publish.sh` refuses to commit on main (mirrors `larch-log.sh commit` guard) — prevents accidental direct-to-main commits.
   119	- **Session ID availability**: `SESSION_ID` is parsed from `session-setup.sh` output in Step 0 and threaded through to Step 5. If empty (edge case in parsing), `design-log-publish.sh` fails fast with `PUBLISH_ERROR=missing-run-id`.
   120	- **DESIGN_TMPDIR symlinks**: skipped during copy (not followed) to prevent infinite loops on any self-referential symlinks.
   121	- **create-pr.sh pre-push dirty-tree guard**: `design-log-publish.sh` ensures the working tree is clean before calling `create-pr.sh` by committing the log files first and not leaving any staged changes.
   122	- **PR already exists**: `create-pr.sh` handles this via its existing-PR fast-path (`PR_STATUS=existing`); merge proceeds on the existing PR number.
   123	
   124	### Failure modes
   125	
   126	1. **`gh pr merge --admin` fails with MERGE_RESULT=policy_denied**: happens when the repo has protection rules that cannot be overridden by `--admin`. Mitigation: `design-log-publish.sh` emits `PUBLISH_OK=false PUBLISH_ERROR=merge-failed`, prints warning, operator can merge manually.
   127	2. **`[skip ci]` not honored by repo CI**: some repos don't support the `[skip ci]` convention. Mitigation: the PR contains only log files under `larch-logs/design/`, so CI will pass trivially (no code changes). `--admin` merge is the primary bypass anyway.
   128	3. **Redaction truncation or failure**: `redact-secrets.sh` is a best-effort pass. If it fails for a file, `design-log-publish.sh` emits `PUBLISH_OK=false PUBLISH_ERROR=redaction-failed` and aborts without committing (fail-closed).
   129	
   130	### Testing strategy
   131	
   132	- `scripts/test-tracking-issue-write.sh`: add `planned` state test + idempotency test (6 new assertions)
   133	- `scripts/test-design-log-publish.sh`: new offline harness (happy path, default-branch guard, dry-run, create-pr failure) with stubbed git/gh
   134	- Manual smoke test: run `/design <issue>` end-to-end; confirm `[PLANNED]` prefix on issue title and PR created at `larch-logs/design/<run-id>/`
   135	
   136	diff_lines: 350

