scripts/validate-research-output.md:3:`scripts/validate-research-output.sh` is the substantive-content validator invoked by `scripts/collect-agent-results.sh --substantive-validation` after the existing non-empty + retry path settles a successful output. Phase 3 of umbrella issue #413 (closes #416, #447, #473). Promotes the documented "caller's responsibility" check (`skills/research/references/research-phase.md`) into a deterministic gate. Substantive = body word count >= `--min-words` (default 200, fenced-code-block interiors excluded) AND (when `--require-citations` is on, the default) at least one provenance marker (file or `file:line` with a recognized extension, including leading-dot hidden files with a basename; extensionless `Makefile`/`Dockerfile`/`GNUmakefile`; fenced code block with >= 1 non-blank content line; URL). Probe 1 is split into two extension tiers per #473 (long-tier: relaxed rule; short-tier: strict path-likeness rule — see "Probe 1 short-extension strict-mode rule (#473)" below). Exit 0 on success; non-zero exits emit a single-line diagnostic on stdout/stderr — 2 (body thin), 3 (no marker), 4 (file missing or not readable), and validation-mode 5 (`CURSOR_EMPTY_RESPONSE`). `--validation-mode` substantive short-circuit: legacy `NO_ISSUES_FOUND` as the entire first non-empty line (case-sensitive), or JSON with `no_issues_found: true` detected by `jq` on that line, then `jq` on the full trimmed non-blank body when the first line begins `{`, then first-JSON-value decode when needed (so pretty-printed objects plus trailing operational notes still match) — trailing content after a recognized sentinel is accepted and preserved; treats the literal `CURSOR_EMPTY_RESPONSE` (matched against the entire trimmed content) as exit 5 so `scripts/collect-agent-results.sh` can emit `STATUS=CURSOR_EMPTY_RESPONSE` instead of generic `STATUS=NOT_SUBSTANTIVE`; and accepts a response containing valid inline TSV records (detected via `validate_structured_tsv`, handles TSV inside code fences) as substantive even when the word-count or citation gates would otherwise fail — this covers cursor plan-mode responses where the TSV sidecar could not be written and TSV rows were inlined in the text output instead. `--structured-reviewer-mode` is an orthogonal validator for reviewer JSONL/TSV records; it exits 0 on valid records or when either no-findings sentinel matches the same first-line JSON / `NO_ISSUES_FOUND` rules as validation mode (trailing content accepted after a recognized sentinel), exits 5 with `structured records not found after repair` when no records validate, and bypasses the prose word-count/citation gates. `--write-structured <path>` writes normalized valid records to that path, or an empty file for either no-findings sentinel and structured failures. JSONL detection uses `jq` when available and falls back to the degraded strict prefix `{"schema_version":1,`; TSV detection requires the exact header and 8 tab-separated fields, repairing extra tabs by folding them into `suggested_fix`. Tilde-fence variants (`~~~`), length-mismatched fences, and adversarial padding are documented limitations. `scripts/test-validate-research-output.sh` is its regression test, wired into `make lint` via the `test-validate-research-output` Makefile target. `scripts/collect-agent-results.sh` translates validator exit 5 under validation mode into `STATUS=CURSOR_EMPTY_RESPONSE`; other non-zero exits become `STATUS=NOT_SUBSTANTIVE` and the validator's diagnostic in `FAILURE_REASON` (sanitized at the collector boundary). Edit-in-sync rule: changes to the marker regex set (long/short tier membership), the fence-stripping word-count rule, the structured schema, or the exit-code numbering must update this contract, the script header (which feeds `--help`), and the regression test in lockstep.
