scripts/implement-finalize.md:110:- Before invoking `kill_session_background_processes` and `cleanup-tmpdir.sh`, teardown finalizes the manifest best-effort, skipped when `RUN_ID` is empty or `REPO_UNAVAILABLE=true`. Before the final status update, teardown probes `$IMPLEMENT_TMPDIR/larch-logs/implement/<RUN_ID>/manifest.json`; when missing, it runs `larch-log.sh init` and immediately tags the synthesized manifest with `status=partial` and `recovery_reason=manifest_lost_mid_run` so a partial run-log directory is identifiable. Manifest finalization on normal paths: when `STALL_TRACKING=true`, sets `stalled_at_step` only (no post-flush `status`/`pr_number` writes on success or design-only teardown). The `larch-log.sh manifest --log-root "$IMPLEMENT_TMPDIR/larch-logs"` call writes the field atomically via temp-and-mv, using `--argjson` for JSON-native values (numbers, booleans, `null`). Teardown does not call `larch-log.sh commit`; committed log flushes are owned by explicit lifecycle flush points.
