skills/fix-issue/SKILL.md:192:For `INTENT=PR`, the launcher MUST pass `--require-plan-block` so `find-lock-issue.sh` runs `plan-block-read.sh` on the resolved lock subject **before** posting `IN PROGRESS` (including the umbrella child-dispatch path — the probe targets the child). For `INTENT=NON_PR`, omit the flag — non-PR work is not gated on an implementation plan block.
skills/fix-issue/SKILL.md:208:The script combines verification, optional **pre-lock plan anchor read** (when `--require-plan-block` is set — delegates to `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/plan-block-read.sh` after the dirty-tree probe and before `issue-lifecycle.sh comment --lock`), local dirty-tree probe, comment-lock acquisition, and best-effort title rename. See `skills/fix-issue/scripts/find-lock-issue.md` for the full stdout contract and exit code semantics (including **exit 6** — `PLAN_PROBE_FAILED=true`, `LOCK_ACQUIRED=false`, no `IN PROGRESS` posted).
skills/fix-issue/SKILL.md:213:  - **Non-umbrella path** (`IS_UMBRELLA` absent or empty): If `RENAMED=false`, the title rename failed best-effort — print `**⚠ 4: find & lock — found and locked #$ISSUE_NUMBER: $ISSUE_TITLE; title rename failed, /implement Branch 2 will retry. (<elapsed>)**`. If the numeric `ISSUE_NUMBER` from this stdout differs from the Step 1 `get-issue-details.sh` target (umbrella child dispatch), re-run `get-issue-details.sh --issue $ISSUE_NUMBER` to refresh `$FIX_ISSUE_TMPDIR/issue-details.txt` before Step 5. Then continue to Step 5.
skills/fix-issue/SKILL.md:214:  - **Umbrella-dispatched path** (`IS_UMBRELLA=true UMBRELLA_ACTION=dispatched`): If `RENAMED=false`, print `**⚠ 4: find & lock — found and locked child #$ISSUE_NUMBER of umbrella #$UMBRELLA_NUMBER: $ISSUE_TITLE; title rename failed, /implement Branch 2 will retry. (<elapsed>)**`. The literal substring `found and locked` is preserved in both sub-cases so callers recognize the success path with a single sentinel — see FINDING_2 from the umbrella-PR code-review panel. Re-run `get-issue-details.sh --issue $ISSUE_NUMBER` to refresh issue details for the **child** before Step 5 — `$ISSUE_NUMBER` refers to the chosen child; downstream `/implement` adopts the CHILD via its **positional** `<issue-N>` tail (not a removed `--issue` flag).
skills/fix-issue/SKILL.md:215:- **Exit 2**: Parse `ERROR` from stdout. Print `**⚠ 4: find & lock — error: $ERROR (<elapsed>)**`. Skip to Step 8. Dirty-tree pre-lock abort is one exit-2 sub-case: operator action is commit or stash local changes, then re-run; no manual unlock is needed because no GitHub state was touched. This differs from a narrow post-lock TOCTOU dirty tree that Step 0 setup's downstream preflight catches after lock acquisition; that path still follows the Stale-IN-PROGRESS recovery guidance below.
skills/fix-issue/SKILL.md:216:- **Exit 3**: Eligibility passed but lock acquisition failed (concurrent runner won the race, or `gh` API failed mid-sequence; for umbrella-dispatched paths, the failure is on the chosen child and the `ERROR` carries umbrella context — `Failed to lock chosen child #C of umbrella #U: <reason>`). Parse `ISSUE_NUMBER` and `ERROR`. Print `**⚠ 4: find & lock — lock failed for #$ISSUE_NUMBER: $ERROR. Another run may have claimed this issue, or the IN PROGRESS comment stream may have been partially mutated — see Known Limitations "Stale IN PROGRESS lock" for recovery before re-running. (<elapsed>)**`. Best-effort terminal summary (no GitHub upsert):
skills/fix-issue/SKILL.md:220:  Skip to Step 8. The remote issue may be left inconsistent (for example, a duplicate-`IN PROGRESS` post-check failure leaves two `IN PROGRESS` comments). Follow manual recovery in Known Limitations "Stale IN PROGRESS lock" before re-running.
skills/fix-issue/SKILL.md:227:- **Exit 6** (PR plan probe failed before lock — `PLAN_PROBE_FAILED=true`, `LOCK_ACQUIRED=false`): parse `ISSUE_NUMBER`, `ISSUE_TITLE`, and optional `MALFORMED=`. No `IN PROGRESS` comment was posted — the issue was never locked by this run. Post a single `gh issue comment` on `#$ISSUE_NUMBER` whose body includes the HTML marker `<!-- larch:plan-missing -->` **and** operator-facing prose that `/implement` requires a valid `larch:plan` block (see `docs/issue-anchored-plan.md`) and that the operator should run `/design $ISSUE_NUMBER` first (include the malformed token when `MALFORMED=` is present). No title restore is required (lock never acquired). Write terminal outcome state and skip to Step 8:
skills/fix-issue/SKILL.md:231:  } > "$FIX_ISSUE_TMPDIR/final-report-state.sh"
skills/fix-issue/SKILL.md:258:After `/implement` completes, capture the PR URL and PR number from its output. Save as `PR_URL` and `PR_NUMBER`. Also parse a `MERGE_RESULT=` line from the same captured stdout when present (`merged`, `admin_merged`, `already_merged`, etc. — same vocabulary as `ship-pr-state.sh`) and export it as shell variable `MERGE_RESULT` for Step 6c.
skills/fix-issue/SKILL.md:262:If `/implement` exits **3** (**Preflight audit refused** — see `skills/implement/SKILL.md` exit-code table): when the refuse path posted a clarify request, print `**⚠ 5: execute — /implement preflight refused (exit 3, clarify posted). Run /design $ISSUE_NUMBER to answer clarify questions, then re-run /fix-issue. Issue #$ISSUE_NUMBER remains locked with IN PROGRESS until the PR path completes or you manually clear the lock.**` When Preflight refused with `STATE=ambiguous` from `clarify-state.sh` (**no** clarify post), print `**⚠ 5: execute — /implement preflight refused (exit 3, clarify-state ambiguous — no clarify posted). Repair the issue comment graph manually, then re-run /fix-issue. Issue #$ISSUE_NUMBER remains locked with IN PROGRESS until resolved or you manually clear the lock.**` Then write `OUTCOME=bailed-implement-preflight-refused` to `$FIX_ISSUE_TMPDIR/final-report-state.sh` (merge with existing keys) and invoke `write-final-report.sh` best-effort; skip to Step 8.
skills/fix-issue/SKILL.md:266:- **Bail detected** (token present): the adopted issue was closed externally after `/fix-issue` locked it. Print `**⚠ 5: execute — /implement bailed: issue #$ISSUE_NUMBER was closed externally after /fix-issue locked it. Cannot recover automatically. (<elapsed>)**`. Do NOT call `issue-lifecycle.sh close` — the issue is already closed and there is no successful run to pair with a DONE comment / PR backfill. **Umbrella finalize hook** (FINDING_8): before skipping to Step 8, if `$UMBRELLA_NUMBER` is set, check whether the externally-closed child was the umbrella's last open child and finalize if so:
skills/fix-issue/SKILL.md:278:   } > "$FIX_ISSUE_TMPDIR/final-report-state.sh"
skills/fix-issue/SKILL.md:282:- **Generic failure** (token absent): print `**⚠ 5: execute — /implement failed. Issue #$ISSUE_NUMBER remains locked with IN PROGRESS comment and [IN PROGRESS] title prefix. (<elapsed>)**`. Then:
skills/fix-issue/SKILL.md:286:   } > "$FIX_ISSUE_TMPDIR/final-report-state.sh"
skills/fix-issue/SKILL.md:289:   Skip to Step 8. The IN PROGRESS comment serves as an indicator that manual intervention is needed. Note: `/implement` Step 18 may have renamed the issue title to `[STALLED] ...` (managed lifecycle prefix); see Known Limitations "Title-prefix interaction on adopted-issue retry" for the recovery flow before re-running `/fix-issue` against the same issue.
skills/fix-issue/SKILL.md:297:If the work cannot be completed (e.g., `/issue` fails repeatedly, the issue's instructions are infeasible, or required external access is unavailable), print `**⚠ 5: execute — non-PR task failed. Issue #$ISSUE_NUMBER remains locked with IN PROGRESS comment and [IN PROGRESS] title prefix. (<elapsed>)**` and skip to Step 8. The IN PROGRESS comment serves as an indicator that manual intervention is needed — same recovery semantics as the `/implement` failure path.
skills/fix-issue/SKILL.md:307:When `/implement` merges the PR (delegation used merge-capable argv per Step 5a), GitHub automatically closes the issue via `Closes #N` in the PR body, and `/implement` Step 12a/12b already renames the title to `[DONE]`. No explicit `issue-lifecycle.sh close` call is needed. Step 6a is a no-op on the PR path — proceed directly to Step 6c.
