skills/implement/scripts/hook-stop-fail-close.md:9:**Post-/bump-version boundary** (issue #1878): blocks session stop when `.bump-version-armed` exists but `postbump-state.sh` does not yet exist. Note: since v26.0.15 the version bump runs inside `ship-pr.sh` (via `classify-bump.sh` and `apply-bump.sh` shell calls) and `check-bump-version.sh --mode pre` is NOT invoked — so `.bump-version-armed` is never written on the normal ship-pr.sh path and this guard is inert for that path. The guard remains for any operator-driven or legacy path that still calls `check-bump-version.sh --mode pre` directly. Recovery (if triggered): complete sub-step 2 silent parse, call `check-bump-version.sh --mode post`, write `postbump-state.sh`, then invoke `implement-finalize.sh postbump`. See NEVER #11 in `skills/implement/SKILL.md` for the current ship-pr.sh contract.
skills/issue/scripts/allocate-candidates.md:12:`--total-items N` is the count of **non-malformed** items in the /issue batch — NOT `ITEMS_TOTAL`. Malformed items (per `parse-input.sh`'s `ITEM_<i>_MALFORMED=true` flag) are excluded from Phase 1/2 and so contribute zero CAND rows; their inclusion in the denominator would understate the per-item floor (e.g. 10 non-malformed + 5 malformed → floor(30/15)=2 instead of the correct floor=3).
skills/issue/scripts/allocate-candidates.md:76:Implemented in Bash 3.2-safe style — no `declare -A` (associative arrays), no `mapfile`, no `${var,,}` lowercasing. macOS `/bin/bash` is 3.2 by default, and other scripts in `skills/issue/scripts/*` follow the same constraint. Uses parallel arrays + `awk` + `sort` for non-trivial state. The regression harness `test-allocate-candidates.sh` includes a `grep -nE 'declare -A|mapfile|\$\{[A-Z_]+,,\}'` check that fails the harness if Bash-4-only constructs creep in.
