skills/issue/scripts/parse-input.md:25:Unlike `/research` (which mitigates via a producer-side body-line backslash escape — prefix `\` on any literal `### Foo` line in finding prose; see `skills/research/scripts/render-findings-batch.md` "Body composition"), **`/umbrella` has no mechanical escape mechanism in `render-batch-input.sh`**: enforcement is documentation/contract-only. The rule is stated at three coordinated surfaces — `skills/umbrella/SKILL.md` Step 3B.1's `body` bullet (prompt-side directive that runs only on the normal-mode pipeline), `skills/umbrella/scripts/render-batch-input.md` "Piece-body item-split hazard" (producer-side contract scoped to the normal-mode pipeline), and this consumer-side catch-all subsection (covers all upstream producers including those that bypass the renderer).
skills/umbrella/scripts/render-umbrella-body.md:9:**Output**: writes `$TMPDIR/umbrella-body.md` (a markdown body with `## Summary` paragraph + `## Children` checklist using GitHub-native `- [ ] #<N> — <title>` rendering). The body file write uses a **checked write + atomic rename** pattern: stage to an unpredictable `mktemp` partial under `$TMPDIR`, verify the partial is non-empty, reject pre-existing non-regular `$OUT` (so a caller-injected directory at the destination cannot make `mv` silently nest the partial inside it on BSD/macOS), then `mv` into place. Consumers see either the fully-written file or no file at all — no truncated intermediate state. An `EXIT` trap installed immediately after the staging `mktemp` succeeds also unlinks the partial on every error-exit path (empty staged body, pre-existing non-regular `$OUT`, `mv` failure), so the caller's `--tmpdir` does not accumulate `umbrella-body.md.*` partials across retries or CI reruns; on the success path the trap is a no-op because `mv` has already moved the partial. Stdout: `UMBRELLA_BODY_FILE=<path>`, `UMBRELLA_TITLE_HINT=<derived>`. Stdout success KVs are emitted ONLY past the `mv` gate — a failed body write produces a non-zero exit with `ERROR=…` on stderr and no `UMBRELLA_BODY_FILE=` / `UMBRELLA_TITLE_HINT=` lines.
